  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two resistors are connected in series across a battery as shown in figure. If a voltmeter of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;is used to measure the potential difference across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resister, the reading of the voltmeter will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0156_234d147a11a4.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 139px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0156_ec4861f84097.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 192px;\" /></p><p>The voltmeter resistance is given to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. The equivalent resistance in the given circuit is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>500</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2000</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2000</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>500</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>600</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p><p>Now, current in the circuit is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>1000</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p>Reading of the voltmeter will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>600</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>1000</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>"
  }
}